e defines the Next.js sitemap, integrating both hardcoded static routes and dynamic routes driven by the database schema. The current implementation fetches data from Drizzle but was examined to troubleshoot potential issues in the indexing structure.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Examining sitemap generation and static routes","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:44:37.721Z","title":"Read sitemap.ts configuration","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpu6vtuk_4b722981be3f":{"concepts":["subagent orchestration","process lifecycle"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Subagent process received stop signal","Timestamp: 2026-05-31T19:45:16.482Z"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpu6vtuk_4b722981be3f","importance":2,"narrative":"The subagent successfully concluded its assigned task and exited. All relevant state updates or side effects should have been finalized prior to this signal.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Completion of secondary task processing","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:45:16.482Z","title":"Subagent execution terminated","type":"subagent"},"obs_mpu6waf6_e122ff9ca6d0":{"concepts":["agent orchestration","task delegation"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Subagent process initiated at 2026-05-31T19:45:37.959Z","Transitioning control to secondary agent context"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpu6waf6_e122ff9ca6d0","importance":4,"narrative":"A subagent has been triggered to handle specific background tasks. This allows for parallel task execution and isolation of operational logic.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Initialization of auxiliary task handler","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:45:37.959Z","title":"Subagent Execution Started","type":"subagent"},"obs_mpu6wigr_9e27436090a6":{"concepts":["SEO Hub and Spoke model","Topical Authority","Internal Linking Architecture","Information Hierarchy"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Pillar pages focus on broad head terms with surface-level breadth","Cluster content provides deep, comprehensive coverage for long-tail keywords","Bidirectional internal linking is required to establish topical authority","Decision threshold for pillar pages: 2,000+ words covering 5+ subtopics"],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpu6wigr_9e27436090a6","importance":5,"narrative":"Fetched authoritative guidance on SEO content architecture to define the relationship between pillar pages and cluster content. This information will inform the content strategy and internal linking structure for the project's information hierarchy.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Researching pillar page vs. cluster content strategies","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:45:48.384Z","title":"Fetched SEO Hub and Spoke Architecture Guidance","type":"web_fetch"},"obs_mpu6wiiv_01c59aeb8fd0":{"concepts":["Topical Authority","Content Strategy","Semantic SEO","Gap Analysis"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Content clusters require a strategic shift from individual posts to semantic ecosystems.","Planning phases include scope definition, roadmap creation (pillar-first vs. spoke-first), and resource allocation.","Key success metrics involve balancing editorial velocity with competitor gap analysis.","Common pitfalls include underestimating research time and failing to schedule content maintenance."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpu6wiiv_01c59aeb8fd0","importance":4,"narrative":"The web search provided a detailed framework for planning cluster content. This blueprint emphasizes the importance of resource allocation and intentional sequencing of pillar and spoke articles to build topical authority.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Researching topical authority and content architecture","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:45:48.462Z","title":"Extracted cluster content planning strategies","type":"web_fetch"},"obs_mpu6woou_f77e2c1540bc":{"concepts":["SEO strategy","Topical authority","Internal linking architecture","Link equity","Semantic relevance"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Internal linking serves as an architectural component for topical authority, not just navigation.","Semantic relevance between linked pages increases the weight of link equity signals.","Anchor text optimization requires a mix of branded, naked, and descriptive phrases.","Orphaned pages should be integrated via high-authority contextual links.","Link equity flows bi-directionally: downstream (pillar to cluster) and upstream (cluster to pillar)."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpu6woou_f77e2c1540bc","importance":4,"narrative":"The agent researched SEO best practices for internal linking to understand how to signal topical authority. The content highlights the importance of semantic relevance, hierarchical structure, and the avoidance of orphaned pages to maintain crawl budget and equity flow.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Researching best practices for site architecture and SEO internal linking","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:45:56.451Z","title":"Extracted content on Internal Linking for Topic Clusters","type":"web_fetch"},"obs_mpu6wzgg_817a8c231f58":{"concepts":["topical authority","content cluster strategy","internal linking architecture","semantic SEO","link equity flow"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Retrieved content from topicalhq.com regarding cluster content planning, internal linking strategies, and pillar-page vs. cluster roles.","Planning emphasizes competitor gap analysis, editorial velocity, and strategic roadmap creation (pillar-first vs. spoke-first).","Internal linking is defined as an architectural tool for distributing link equity and signaling semantic relevance rather than just navigation.","Cluster strength relies on semantic relevance of internal links rather than raw link counts."],"files":[],"id":"obs_mpu6wzgg_817a8c231f58","importance":4,"narrative":"The subagent successfully fetched and parsed three detailed guides on topical authority. The content highlights the importance of strategic roadmap planning and architectural internal linking to build semantic authority in search engines.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Retrieved 3 articles on cluster content planning and internal linking","timestamp":"2026-05-31T19:46:10.405Z","title":"Fetched topical authority guide articles","type":"subagent"},"obs_mpwzaifa_f9ccfd72e7a9":{"concepts":["context window optimization","token management","dependency removal"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["User requested removal of 'agentmemory' module.","Reasoning provided is excessive token consumption without perceived utility."],"files":["src/agentmemory.ts","src/index.ts"],"id":"obs_mpwzaifa_f9ccfd72e7a9","importance":6,"narrative":"The user has decided to discontinue the use of the agentmemory component, citing high token overhead relative to the value provided. I must identify and remove all references, imports, and initialization logic related to agentmemory to optimize the context window.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Optimizing context window usage","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:36:03.118Z","title":"Removal of agentmemory integration","type":"decision"},"obs_mpwzammu_79c09b7354fb":{"concepts":["MCP server","token optimization","configuration management"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Removed agentmemory MCP server from settings.","Configuration updated successfully via update-config skill."],"files":["settings.json"],"id":"obs_mpwzammu_79c09b7354fb","importance":4,"narrative":"The agentmemory MCP server was removed from the configuration settings to reduce unnecessary token consumption during AI interactions. This change restricts the available tools to Read-only operations for this context.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Optimizing token usage by pruning MCP servers","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:36:08.574Z","title":"Remove agentmemory MCP server configuration","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpwzaqk1_a670168c6c05":{"concepts":["Claude configuration","plugin architecture","environment settings"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Active plugins: warp@claude-code-warp and agentmemory@agentmemory","Configured marketplaces point to GitHub repositories: warpdotdev/claude-code-warp and rohitg00/agentmemory","Dangerous mode permission prompt is disabled (skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt: true)"],"files":["/Users/torel/.claude/settings.json"],"id":"obs_mpwzaqk1_a670168c6c05","importance":3,"narrative":"Read the global Claude configuration file to understand enabled plugins and environment settings. The configuration confirms that custom plugins are active and the agent is configured to skip safety prompts for dangerous operations.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Inspection of ~/.claude/settings.json","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:36:13.657Z","title":"Read Claude configuration settings","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpwzaum0_ca9617bdd0f5":{"concepts":["Claude CLI configuration","Plugin management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Removed 'agentmemory@agentmemory' from 'enabledPlugins'","Removed 'agentmemory' entry from 'extraKnownMarketplaces'","Retained 'warp@claude-code-warp' configuration"],"files":["/Users/torel/.claude/settings.json"],"id":"obs_mpwzaum0_ca9617bdd0f5","importance":4,"narrative":"The agent modified the local Claude configuration file to remove the agentmemory plugin. This change deactivates the plugin and cleans up its associated repository metadata from the settings.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Updating .claude/settings.json to disable the agentmemory plugin","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:36:18.912Z","title":"Remove agentmemory plugin configuration","type":"file_edit"},"obs_mpwzbuq5_5c3cbb26cfc4":{"concepts":["macOS LaunchAgents","persistence mechanisms","background services"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Found /Users/torel/Library/LaunchAgents/com.agentmemory.plist","No matches found in LaunchDaemons","Search scope included claude and agentmemory naming patterns"],"files":["/Users/torel/Library/LaunchAgents/com.agentmemory.plist"],"id":"obs_mpwzbuq5_5c3cbb26cfc4","importance":5,"narrative":"The system scanned for persistent background tasks related to agent memory management. A specific configuration file for agentmemory was identified in the user's LaunchAgents directory, indicating an active background process.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Checking LaunchAgents for agentmemory related plists","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:37:05.713Z","title":"Search for persistent background processes","type":"command_run"},"obs_mpwzbvbo_6ab95a48cace":{"concepts":["system configuration","directory traversal","MCP architecture"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Identified core configuration files: settings.json, mcp-needs-auth-cache.json","Discovered persistent task data stored in ~/.claude/tasks/ subdirectory","Plugins are managed under ~/.claude/plugins/ with catalog and installation caches"],"files":["~/.claude/settings.json","~/.claude/mcp-needs-auth-cache.json"],"id":"obs_mpwzbvbo_6ab95a48cace","importance":3,"narrative":"Inspected the ~/.claude directory to map the internal storage structure and configuration management. This confirms where settings, MCP auth states, and task-specific history are located, providing context for future configuration edits.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Probing the ~/.claude directory structure","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:37:06.490Z","title":"List and explore Claude configuration files","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpwzby5y_ed5a79991a0a":{"concepts":["macOS LaunchAgent","plist","environment variables","service persistence"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Service label: com.agentmemory","Executable: /Users/torel/.nvm/versions/node/v22.14.0/bin/agentmemory","Environment variables: AGENTMEMORY_III_VERSION 0.16.0, AGENTMEMORY_INJECT_CONTEXT true, GRAPH_EXTRACTION_ENABLED true, AGENTMEMORY_AUTO_COMPRESS true","Logs redirected to ~/.local/share/agentmemory/","Persistence: RunAtLoad and KeepAlive are enabled"],"files":["/Users/torel/Library/LaunchAgents/com.agentmemory.plist"],"id":"obs_mpwzby5y_ed5a79991a0a","importance":5,"narrative":"The agent read the plist configuration file to understand the runtime environment and startup parameters of the agentmemory service. This revealed critical configuration flags, including memory auto-compression settings and the specific Gemini model in use.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Inspecting macOS LaunchAgent configuration for agentmemory service","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:37:10.175Z","title":"Read agentmemory launch agent configuration","type":"file_read"},"obs_mpwzbyde_482e0dd82c22":{"concepts":["plugin management","configuration file","environment discovery"],"confidence":1,"facts":["System has two plugins installed: claude-code-warp (v2.1.0) and agentmemory (v0.9.24)","Plugins are located in ~/.claude/plugins/cache/","Configuration schema version is 2"],"files":["~/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json"],"id":"obs_mpwzbyde_482e0dd82c22","importance":3,"narrative":"The agent inspected the installed plugins configuration to verify environment state. It confirmed the versions and installation paths of the active plugins, providing context for available tool capabilities.","sessionId":"b373fd99-6539-4e8d-b28f-129affedacdd","subtitle":"Inspection of ~/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json","timestamp":"2026-06-02T18:37:10.440Z","title":"Read installed Claude plugins configuration","type":"file_read"}}␀␀␀­*␀Puÿÿ